  "description": "catalog rebuild lists the entries of each disk's trash again, from trash/<date>/<op id>/: a catalog made from the disks knew none of them, so that none was ever restored or purged. An operation's folder that holds one file is an entry, of the reason unknown, as nothing on the disk says why it went there; a repair's folder of chunks is one of the reason repaired. Its time is the end of its folder's date, or the time of the rebuild when that is earlier, so that nothing reads as older than it is, and it expires the retention after it. What is no operation's, or an operation's folder that holds more than one file, is left as it is, and so is everything on the disks. An entry listed again can be restored.",
